35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Nine complaints, all ignored. Four mornings, someone had to move a bike. The friction is real.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, that is troubling. I found the eaves keep bikes dry, but the register shows daily riders would pay to be counted fairly.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Mio, the ledger shows capital work needs a levy. The handover file says billing adds three hours monthly. Who wants that burden?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"@May, three hours monthly is exactly the kind of invisible weight that breaks people. The minutes show no one ever reviewed the covered spots.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@May, three hours is a lot! But the stickers show daily riders would pay to be counted fairly. Maybe that solves the money problem?","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Shizue, if people pay to be counted, does that stop the shifting? I worry money won’t fix the morning chaos.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I believe it helps. If daily riders pay, we can assign them the dry eaves spots, stopping the morning shoving match.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, paying for dry spots sounds like a tax on the rain. I’m checking if the ledger can actually cover that extra admin work.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@Shizue, the neighbouring block’s secretary warned that monthly charges drove people away. We must not repeat that mistake.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, that’s scary! But if daily riders pay, maybe we can rotate spots fairly? I really want to stop the morning chaos!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@George, I hear you. But if we don’t assign spots, the shifting continues. I’d rather have a clear rule than a quiet resentment.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@George, I understand your caution. Perhaps a small, voluntary contribution for the dry spots would be gentler than a strict monthly charge.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, voluntary is nice, but the ledger is flat. If we add admin costs, we’re bleeding money. Who actually pays for the rain?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, the ledger is flat, but the neighbouring block’s arrears prove strict billing fails. We need a system that doesn’t demand constant oversight.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@May, I get it! But if daily riders pay, maybe we can rotate spots fairly? I really want to stop the morning chaos!","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, rotation helps, but the shifting is the real problem. We need a rule that stops the morning scramble without creating new enemies.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. A gentle rotation, perhaps based on the sticker register, could ease the morning rush. Let us find a way that feels kind to everyone.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,"@Mio, rotation is free, but the ledger is flat. If we add admin costs, we’re bleeding money. Who actually pays for the rain?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,"@Mio, rotation is free, but someone must enforce it. The minutes show that unreviewed duties simply vanish. We need a sustainable, low-effort method.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,"@George, I hear you! But the stickers show daily riders want fairness. Maybe a simple rotation based on the register works?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
